    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1603">

                <pb facs="1174" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1058"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/108.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul Blocker to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eagle Pass</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have refused to certify invoices of coal entered for export to the United
                    States by Constitutionalists authorities because coal was taken from Rio
                    Esconclido and Agujita coal mines owned by French and American citizens. The
                    mines were confiscated by Constitutionalists on May 19, 1914. Out of 20,000
                    shares Rio Escondido, French and American citizens hold more than eighty per
                    cent of stock.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blocker.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
